      "Before the cards, referees gave warnings and sent players off with words alone. This worked well enough when everyone on the field spoke the same language, but international matches made things much more difficult. At the 1966 World Cup in England, a referee from West Germany sent off the captain of Argentina during a match against England. The captain did not seem to understand the decision, and for several minutes he refused to leave the field while his teammates argued angrily around him.",
