    qa: [
      { q: 'Why was the cross of the groma mounted on a short bracket?', choices: ['So that the cords would not swing in the wind.', 'So that the staff would not block the surveyor\'s view.', 'So that the assistant could carry it more easily.', 'So that it could measure differences in height.'], answer: 1, why: '第3段落で、十字は柱が測量師の視線をさえぎらないように短い腕木に取りつけられていたと述べられている。' },
      { q: 'What does the writer say about the square townships of the United States?', choices: ['They were copied directly from Roman bronze maps.', 'They were laid out by surveyors who used a groma.', 'They were designed to settle Roman legal quarrels.', 'They shared the Roman idea but were not descended from it.'], answer: 3, why: '第6段落で、アメリカのタウンシップはローマの方式の直接の子孫ではないが、幾何学的な模様で土地を管理しやすくするという同じ考えにもとづいていたと述べられている。' },
    ],
