    qa: [
      { q: 'Why did rammed earth decline in industrialised countries?', choices: ['Its walls were found to be weaker than stone walls.', 'Soil suitable for building had become very hard to find.', 'Modern materials were quicker to build with using fewer workers.', 'Cointeraux\'s booklets made the technique seem too complicated.'], answer: 2, why: '第5段落で、れんがやコンクリートは大量生産でき少人数ですばやく組み立てられたが、版築は時間と重労働を必要としたと述べている。' },
      { q: 'What does the saying about good boots and a good hat refer to?', choices: ['Workers wearing protective clothing while pounding the soil.', 'Protecting earth walls from water above and below.', 'Adding cement to the soil to make walls stronger.', 'Building walls only in the dry regions of the northwest.'], answer: 1, why: '第7段落で、石の土台が湿った地面から、広い屋根が雨から壁を守ることを指すと説明している。' },
    ],
