    qa: [
      { q: 'How do geologists use erratics to learn the direction of ice movement?', choices: ['By measuring how deep the scratches on each stone are.', 'By tracing stones back to the place they came from.', 'By comparing the size of boulders on different farms.', 'By counting the atoms that formed inside each rock.'], answer: 1, why: '第5段落：珍しい岩石の石を出どころまでたどり、氷の動いた方向に並ぶ岩の列を見つけることで、氷床の道すじがわかると述べている。' },
      { q: 'Why does the writer say that dating erratics has become important?', choices: ['It shows how many floods the land has experienced.', 'It proves that icebergs once floated over Europe.', 'It reveals where the rare atoms first came from.', 'It helps explain how fast ice sheets can shrink.'], answer: 3, why: '第6段落：こうした年代は氷床がどれほど速く縮みうるかを理解する助けとなり、温暖化する世界で急を要する問題だと述べている。' },
    ],
