    title: 'Why Young Sunflowers Follow the Sun',
    level: '難関大（評論）',
    paragraphs: [
      "Many people believe that sunflowers turn their faces to follow the sun all day long. This is only partly true. Young sunflower plants really do move with the sun, but fully grown sunflowers usually stop moving and face in one direction. Scientists have studied these plants carefully to find out how the movement works and why it changes as the plants grow older.",
      "On a sunny day, the top of a young sunflower faces east in the morning, toward the rising sun. During the day it slowly turns, and by the evening it faces west. Then, during the night, it turns back toward the east, so it is ready for the sunrise the next morning. This daily movement is easy to see if you take photos of a field of young plants every few hours.",
      "A plant does not have muscles, so how can it move? The answer is growth. During the day, the east side of the stem grows faster than the west side, and this makes the stem bend toward the west. At night, the west side grows faster, and the stem slowly bends back toward the east. Scientists also found that the plants have a kind of inner clock. When young sunflowers were moved indoors under a light that did not move, they kept turning in the same daily pattern for a few days.",
      "Following the sun seems to help young plants grow. In one experiment, scientists tied some plants so that they could not turn. These plants grew a little less than plants that were free to move, probably because the moving plants caught more sunlight on their leaves during the day and could make more food.",
      "When a sunflower becomes fully grown and its flower opens, its stem no longer grows quickly, and the movement ends. Most grown flowers face east. This also seems to be useful. Flowers that face east warm up faster in the morning sun, and bees and other insects visit warm flowers more often. When scientists turned some flowers to face west, these flowers received fewer visits from insects. ( A ), when the scientists used a small heater to warm some west-facing flowers in the morning, the number of visits went up.",
      "The sunflower shows that a plant can change its behavior as it grows older. A young plant moves in order to collect light for growing, while an older plant stays still in order to welcome insects. Both of these habits help the sunflower to produce seeds for the next generation.",
    ],
