    id: 'adv-pen-cap-holes',
    title: 'Why Do Many Pen Caps Have a Hole?',
    level: '難関大（評論）',
    paragraphs: [
      "Take the cap off an ordinary ballpoint pen and look at the top of it. On many pens, you will find a small hole there, or a gap between the cap and its clip. It is easy to suppose that the hole is meant to stop the ink from drying out, or to make the cap easier to push on. The most important reason, however, is a more serious one. The hole is there to help keep people alive.",
      "Many people chew pen caps while they are thinking, and children in particular sometimes put them in their mouths. Every so often, a cap is accidentally breathed in and becomes stuck in the airway. This is a real emergency, because a cap that blocks the windpipe can stop a person from breathing. Doctors have reported such cases over the years, and many of them involved children and teenagers. If the cap has a hole in it, some air may still be able to pass through while the person waits for help.",
      "For this reason, many pen makers began to design caps with holes or channels. An international safety standard for the caps of pens and similar writing tools was introduced in the 1990s. For caps that are small enough to be breathed in, it requires that a certain amount of air can still pass through. Some companies are also reported to have used vented caps before then. ( A ), a feature that most people never notice has become a normal part of pen design in many countries.",
      "This does not mean that a pen cap with a hole is safe to swallow or to breathe in. Doctors still treat such accidents as emergencies, and a cap stuck in the airway usually has to be removed in hospital. The hole simply gives a person a better chance of getting enough air until that can happen. It is an example of designing for a rare accident, rather than assuming that the product will always be used properly. Parents are still advised to keep small objects like pen caps away from young children, whatever their design.",
      "There is one more hole on some ballpoint pens, and it has a different purpose. A tiny hole in the side of the barrel lets air in as the ink is used, so that the pressure inside the pen stays the same as the pressure outside. Without it, some pens might not write smoothly. Next time you hold a pen, look carefully at its small holes. They show how much careful thinking can go into even the cheapest object on your desk.",
    ],
