    qa: [
      { q: 'Why does the note rise after stirring stops?', choices: ['The water slowly becomes much hotter', 'The spoon taps the cup more strongly', 'The powder sinks to the bottom of the cup', 'Bubbles escape and sound travels faster'], answer: 3, why: '第5段落 As their number falls ... sound travels through it faster, and the note climbs higher。' },
      { q: 'Why do bubbles slow down sound in a liquid?', choices: ['They make it more squeezable', 'They make the liquid much heavier', 'They make the liquid change color', 'They keep the liquid from moving'], answer: 0, why: '第3段落 because the bubbles make the liquid much easier to squeeze。' },
    ],
