      "Visitors to Nara Park are often surprised by the deer. More than a thousand of them walk freely among old temples, gift shops and crowds of tourists, and many come close to people in the hope of getting something to eat. For many travellers, feeding the deer is one of the most memorable parts of a trip to Nara. But why do so many wild animals live in the middle of a city, and how do people and deer share the same space?",
