    tf: [
      { statement: '空港の免税の買い物は、アイルランドのシャノン空港で始まったと言われることが多い。', answer: true, why: '第2段落 is often said to have begun at Shannon Airport in Ireland in the late 1940s。' },
      { statement: '日本では、1999年に到着ロビーの免税店が廃止されたと言われている。', answer: false, why: '第2段落 1999年に終わったのはヨーロッパ連合の加盟国のあいだの免税販売で、日本は2017年から到着ロビーの免税店をみとめたとある。' },
      { statement: '支持する人々は、店の家賃が着陸料や航空券の値段を低くたもつのに役立つと言っている。', answer: true, why: '第3段落 this income helps to keep landing fees and ticket prices lower。' },
      { statement: '筆者は、空港の免税店を完全に廃止するべきだと考えている。', answer: false, why: '第7段落 airports should keep their duty-free shops / without abolishing it。' },
    ],
    qa: [
      { q: 'Why do critics object to the sale of alcohol and tobacco?', choices: ['Their taxes partly protect public health', 'They are too heavy to carry on board', 'They are mostly produced in other countries', 'Their prices change too often at airports'], answer: 0, why: '第4段落 products whose high taxes are intended in part to protect public health。' },
      { q: 'According to the fifth paragraph, why may some duty-free prices be high?', choices: ['Travellers buy only expensive brands there', 'Airlines add a fee to every purchase', 'Shops pay high rents at airports', 'Governments set the prices for the shops'], answer: 2, why: '第5段落 Because the shops pay high rents and have customers who cannot easily compare prices elsewhere。' },
    ],
